-- The 2000-badge catalogue.
--
-- Supplied as a spreadsheet (Unplug_2000_Unique_Gamification_Badges.xlsx):
-- 2000 unique codes across 152 categories, every row with a code, emoji,
-- label, description and category. Verified before generating this file —
-- no duplicate codes, no blank fields, no characters outside [A-Za-z0-9_] in
-- any code, and every value inside the existing column limits (longest code
-- 36 of 60, label 48 of 120, emoji 4 of 10, category 28 of 30). So no schema
-- change was needed; these are simply rows.
--
-- ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING is the important part.
--
-- Migrations re-run on EVERY deploy here, with no tracking table. An upsert
-- would therefore reset every badge an admin had edited — relabelled,
-- recategorised, disabled — back to the spreadsheet on the next deploy, and
-- it would happen silently. Seeding only what is missing means the catalogue
-- is installed once and belongs to the admin from then on.
--
-- The consequence to know: correcting a typo in this file will NOT update a
-- badge that already exists. That is deliberate. Edit it in the admin, which
-- is the one place badge wording is owned.


ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;

ON CONFLICT (code) DO NOTHING;
